**VERDICT: APPROVE WITH REQUIRED CHANGES. Revise before building.**

Reviewed revision 7, blob `8d1fc4f2`. No files changed or experiments run.

1. **STILL OPEN — Filler damage, partly fixed.** The new reference repairs stage 2. Stage 1 detects filler damage only through fewer correct items, while its benefit test also uses margin ratios. Equal item counts with damaged margins escape the guard. Apply the same outcome definition to benefit and damage. [Design:297](/C:/Users/ethan/Documents/fly-chess-research/documentation/design/neural-learning/replay-diary-memory-design-2026-11-17.md:297)
2. **RESOLVED — Unknown boards.** Fixed denominators and conservative paired comparisons address the exclusion bias in both stages. [Design:315](/C:/Users/ethan/Documents/fly-chess-research/documentation/design/neural-learning/replay-diary-memory-design-2026-11-17.md:315), [Design:351](/C:/Users/ethan/Documents/fly-chess-research/documentation/design/neural-learning/replay-diary-memory-design-2026-11-17.md:351)
3. **RESOLVED — Learning rate.** The redundant sweep and tuning claim are removed. [Design:283](/C:/Users/ethan/Documents/fly-chess-research/documentation/design/neural-learning/replay-diary-memory-design-2026-11-17.md:283)

**New findings**

1. **required-BUILD — The new reference has contradictory starting-state rules.**  
   **Evidence:** “No old replays” skips every old-lesson replay but also “starts each later block in exactly the diary arm’s state.” [Design:269](/C:/Users/ethan/Documents/fly-chess-research/documentation/design/neural-learning/replay-diary-memory-design-2026-11-17.md:269)  
   **Consequence:** in stage 1, skipping replays during the second block can change the third block’s starting state. Restoring the diary’s state would silently import its earlier replay benefit.  
   **Smallest fix:** specify a cumulative control with equality only before the first intervention. If separate block effects are intended, declare separate branches from matched snapshots.

2. **required-BUILD — The failure summary contradicts the revised prerequisite.**  
   **Evidence:** stage 2 now requires forgetting in “no old replays,” but section 8 still dismisses the claim whenever **no diary** retains the earlier lesson. [Design:319](/C:/Users/ethan/Documents/fly-chess-research/documentation/design/neural-learning/replay-diary-memory-design-2026-11-17.md:319), [Design:359](/C:/Users/ethan/Documents/fly-chess-research/documentation/design/neural-learning/replay-diary-memory-design-2026-11-17.md:359)  
   **Consequence:** the two rules can give opposite verdicts because those arms acquire the earlier lesson differently.  
   **Smallest fix:** make section 8 reference the no-old-replays prerequisite.

**Strongest supportable sentence, conditional on passing:** “With the diary absent during scoring, replay-assisted training retained earlier chess-pair rankings better than the specified controls and scored higher on the registered all-legal measure.”
